<%# The shared page header, like every other admin page.

    This page and #edit were the only two in the app that never adopted `components/ui/_page_header`. What
    that cost, measured rather than asserted:

    - **No h1.** The admin layout renders a visually hidden one from the last breadcrumb unless the page
      declares :own_heading, which only the header partial does - so the page's accessible name was "New",
      and the title on screen was an `h2`. A page title at `text-2xl font-bold` in an h2 is the shape the
      header partial exists to stop.
    - **A card inside a card.** `_form` renders its own `.tw-card`, so wrapping it here put two surfaces
      around one form and stacked their padding: 48px before the first field at every width.
    - **The gap above the card was 0px**, because the card was the first thing after the breadcrumb. The
      page rhythm design.md states three times - a 24px header block, and nothing else in that gap - could
      not apply to a page with no header.
    - The heading also carried the card's own `mb-6` *and* a `mb-6` on the outer card, so the section title
      inside sat 24px + 24px + 24px below the breadcrumb. %>
<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
  <%= admin_breadcrumbs(@breadcrumbs) %>

  <%= render layout: "components/ui/page_header",
             locals: { title: "New portfolio transaction" } do %><% end %>

  <%= render "form", portfolio_transaction: @portfolio_transaction %>
</div>
